# oracle: store/local of bond_style bpm/spring (native: b332f28 as the installed lmp, BPM package), cut down from
# examples/bpm/impact/in.bpm.impact.spring: a chain of 4 atoms (3 bonds, atom_style bond) pulled apart at the ends with
# bond_coeff 1 1.0 0.04 1.0 (k, epsilon_c, gamma), bond_style bpm/spring store/local brkbond 10 time id1 id2; the broken
# bonds are written by dump local f_brkbond[1..3] every 10 steps; 300 steps.
# oracle-files: w144bpm_spring_store_broken.dump
# measured: max relative error 2.3e-15 over the thermo rows and the per-atom state (native b332f28 = installed lmp, BPM package)
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=all rel=1e-8 abs=1e-10
units lj
dimension 3
boundary f f f
atom_style bond
newton on off
comm_modify vel yes cutoff 2.6
region box block -10 10 -10 10 -10 10
create_box 1 box bond/types 1 extra/bond/per/atom 4
create_atoms 1 single -1.0 0.0 0.0
create_atoms 1 single 0.0 0.0 0.0
create_atoms 1 single 1.0 0.0 0.0
create_atoms 1 single 2.0 0.0 0.0
mass 1 1.0
create_bonds single/bond 1 1 2
create_bonds single/bond 1 2 3
create_bonds single/bond 1 3 4
group left id 1
group right id 4
velocity left set -0.25 0.0 0.0
velocity right set 0.6 0.0 0.0
pair_style bpm/spring
pair_coeff 1 1 1.0 1.0 1.0
neighbor 0.3 bin
special_bonds lj 0.0 1.0 1.0 coul 1.0 1.0 1.0
bond_style bpm/spring store/local brkbond 10 time id1 id2
bond_coeff 1 1.0 0.04 1.0
fix 1 all nve
compute nb all nbond/atom
compute tb all reduce sum c_nb
dump 2 all local 10 w144bpm_spring_store_broken.dump f_brkbond[1] f_brkbond[2] f_brkbond[3]
thermo_style custom step ke pe ebond c_tb
thermo_modify format float %.15g norm no lost ignore lost/bond ignore
timestep 0.01
thermo 50
run 300
